meta {
  name: List Bug Reports (Producer Rejected)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/bug-reports
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

tests {
  test("returns 403 Forbidden", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(403);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /platform/bug-reports — the producer must not read the queue

  Sent with the **collection-level bearer** (`auth: inherit`), which is the
  producer captured by `Auth/Login` — not `platformAccessToken`. That is the
  whole point of the request.

  This is the assertion that the feature's asymmetry holds. `POST /bug-reports`
  deliberately requires **no permission**, so every producer can file a report;
  reading them back is `platform:bugs:read`, which no agency role holds and
  which `grantsAllEnabledModules` cannot expand into (it only expands
  `{module}:read` / `{module}:write`). A producer reaching this endpoint would
  see every other tenant's reports, including the screens and data they name.

  `403`, not `404`: the route exists and the caller is authenticated: they simply
  are not a platform operator. The non-disclosure rules that make an
  out-of-scope *record* answer 404 (see `Leads/Get Lead (Foreign Lead)`) are
  about hiding whether a specific record exists, which does not apply to a
  collection endpoint.

  ## Errors
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `platform:bugs:read`. Any agency role.
}
